## Compatibility
Originally written for PostgreSQL, this script can be adapted to other SQL dialects and database systems.

Simply ask an AI tool of your choice to modify the query to make it compatible with your preferred SQL dialect or database system. Always review and test the adapted version before execution.

## Limitations & Notes
- Scans base tables only; views are excluded.
- Compares records using all columns within each table.
- Excludes specified system, temporary, and TOAST schemas.
- Only tables containing duplicate groups appear in the database-wide report.
- Requires sufficient database access privileges.
- Large databases and tables may require considerable execution time and resources.
- Tables without columns or tables that cannot be accessed may not produce results.
- The duplicate record details query works on one specified table at a time.
- The schema and table names in the duplicate record details section must be manually specified.
- Uses temporary tables that disappear when the database session ends.
- Does not modify, delete, or clean existing database records.
- Duplicate records are identified based on exact equality across all columns.
- Records that differ in even one column are not considered duplicates.
- The database-wide scanner calculates excess duplicate rows, while the details query retrieves every record belonging to duplicate groups.

## Disclaimer
This script is intended for database inspection, profiling, and duplicate record detection. It does not automatically remove, merge, or modify duplicate records.
